        "text": "Dapps rely on smart contracts on a distributed network to function unlike standard mobile apps that rely on centralized systems. Similar to smart contracts, dapps are open source, meaning anyone can verify, use, copy, and modify the source code. All information of dapps is cryptographically secured and stored on a public, decentralized blockchain maintained by a network of nodes. Another characteristic of dapps is that they can be accessed with a cryptographic token. Today, DApps generally refer to all applications with smart contract functionalities running on blockchain networks. You can think of smart contracts as a core component of dapps. While dapps are the product that provide a complete application experience to users.",
